              "summary": "**Analyzing predictive models**\n\nI have some distinct observations here! I think combining forecasts through averaging creates an ensemble, which might depend on total evidence for proper scoring. Reporting a probability seems essential. For Bayesian pooling, each posterior should be treated as independent private evidence to ensure proper calibration. Although the displayed probabilities might not exactly match due to analysts using more information, I still need to keep confidence statements in mind while combining odds. I also need to avoid double-counting my previous forecast!**Calculating probabilities**\n\nI should mention that I’m combining independent peer posteriors without any hidden observations. I need to check if the confidence probability of the recommended state is correct. For A, converting pB = 1 - c is the next step. I’ve got some odds calculations here. \n\nCalculating ratios like m1 and m3 helped confirm values. I find it interesting that our peer factors contribute to the overall product. I’ll summarize in JSON format once I finalize the probabilities.",
